{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kb4tmV381BsAETewVwDz5j","type":"tool_result","content":"# Leapmotor B05 variants in Australia\n\n**Note:** The full sentences are longer than the 125-character limit, so the quotes below are trimmed excerpts.\n\n| | **Style** | **Design Long Range** |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Price** | $35,990 drive-away | $39,990 drive-away |\n| **Battery** | 56.2kWh LFP | 67.1kWh LFP |\n| **WLTP range** | 401 km | 482 km |\n| **Peak DC** | 174kW (attribution unclear) | 174kW (attribution unclear) |\n| **AC** | 11kW | 11kW |\n| **DC charge claim** | 30–80% in about 16 min | 30–80% in about 18 min |\n\n**Supporting quotes**\n- Price: \"Pricing for the Leapmotor B05 starts from $35,990 for the Style with a drive-away offer, and $39,990 for the Design LR\"\n- Price conditions: \"available on models bought in Lightning Yellow and delivered between 1 July and 30 September, or while stocks last\"\n- Battery: \"The B05 Style features a 56.2kWh lithium iron phosphate (LFP) battery\" and \"the Design LR boosts a bigger 67.1kWh LFP battery\"\n- Range: \"up to 401 kilometres (WLTP) for the Style and up to 482km for the Design LR\"\n- AC: \"Both models support 11kW AC charging\"\n- DC time: \"charging from 30 to 80 per cent in approximately 16 minutes for the Style and 18 minutes for the Design LR\"\n- DC peak: \"thanks to fast charging up to 174kW\"\n  - Sentence structure suggests 174kW covers both models, but it's not stated per variant.\n\n**Sales status**\n- The B05 isn't described as on sale or as having orders open.\n- The article is forward-looking: it \"will arrive in Australian dealerships in late August\" and \"would soon be available in Australia.\"\n- Pricing is called \"a special introductory offer.\"\n- The article is dated 2 July 2026. The page shows 18 November 2026, by which point the 30 September delivery window had passed.\n\n**Price source**\n- Pricing is credited to \"Chinese electric carmaker Leapmotor