{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T57c6PzKD3g84hJLiRAWTa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Hongqi E-HS9 Australia price WLTP range DC charging kW\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2027 Hongqi E-HS9 Targets Sub-$150,000 Australian Price With $10,000 Cashback Offer\",\"url\":\"https://carsauce.com/news/2027-hongqi-hq-e-hs9-australia-price-specs-launch\"},{\"title\":\"Chinese luxury EV brand Hongqi launches in Australia with massive six-seat electric SUV - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2026/11/12/chinese-luxury-ev-brand-hongqi-launches-in-australia-with-massive-six-seat-electric-suv/\"},{\"title\":\"Hongqi launches in Australia as HQ with E-HS9 electric SUV\",\"url\":\"https://autotalk.com.au/industry-news/hongqi-launches-in-australia-as-hq-with-e-hs9-electric-suv\"},{\"title\":\"Hongqi E-HS9 99kWh Price in Australia with Specs 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.autoswheeler.com/vehicles/hongqi-/hongqi-e-hs9-99kwh-price-in-australia-762\"},{\"title\":\"Hongqi enters Australia with E-HS9 expected below A$150,000 (~$103,100) before on-road costs - The Electric Viking\",\"url\":\"https://theelectricviking.com/hongqi-enters-australia-e-hs9-expected-below-a150000-103100-road-costs/\"},{\"title\":\"HongQi enters Australia’s luxury EV market with the E-HS9 flagship electric SUV\",\"url\":\"https://drivenwomenmag.com/2026/11/hongqi-enters-australias-luxury-ev-market/\"},{\"title\":\"Hongqi arrives in Australia with bold E-HS9 luxury electric SUV - Exhaust Notes Australia\",\"url\":\"https://www.exhaustnotes.com.au/hongqi-arrives-in-australia-with-bold-e-hs9-luxury-electric-suv/\"},{\"title\":\"Hongqi E-HS9 designed by former Rolls-Royce design chief now in Australia - The Supercar Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.thesupercarblog.com/hongqi-e-hs9-designed-by-former-rolls-royce-design-chief-now-in-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Hongqi E-HS9 Exclusive specifications\",\"url\":\"https://evkx.net/models/hongqi/e-hs9/e-hs9_exclusive/specifications/\"},{\"title\":\"Hongqi E-HS9 2026 Review, Specs, Price and Mileage (Brochure) - Auto User Manual\",\"url\":\"https://autousermanual.com/blogs/hongqi-e-hs9-2026-review-specs-price-and-mileage-brochure/\"}]\n\nSeveral Australian outlets covering the 11 November 2026 launch agree on the E-HS9's price, range and charging figures.\n\n**Price**\n- Hongqi is selling under the HQ name in Australia. The 2027 E-HS9 has an indicative price below $150,000 before on-road costs, and pre-orders get up to $10,000 cashback.\n- This is not the final price. It's an indicative MSRP before on-road costs, with final pricing still to come. HQ plans one drive-away price per state.\n- Customer deliveries are planned from January 18, 2027.\n\n**Range**\n- A 120 kWh NMC battery gives a claimed WLTP range of 548 km. CATL supplies the battery.\n\n**Charging**\n- It runs on a 400-volt system, and DC fast charging tops out at 140 kW.\n- Hongqi says 10 to 80 per cent takes 48 minutes, and three-phase AC charging goes up to 11 kW. The ports are Type 2 and CCS2.\n\n**Other specs**\n- Dual-motor all-wheel drive makes 411kW and 606Nm, with a claimed 0–100km/h time of 5.5 seconds and a 200km/h top speed.\n- First owners get a 10-year, one million km battery warranty, a seven-year warranty on the rest of the car, and a year of free charging at HQ dealerships.\n\n**Rivals (from CarSauce)**\n- The 2027 Volvo EX90 Ultra Twin Motor Performance costs $134,990 before on-road costs. It has a smaller 111kWh battery but a longer claimed WLTP range of 570km.\n- The 2027 Kia EV9 GT-Line AWD costs $121,000 before on-road costs.\n\n**Older figures to ignore:** Some aggregator sites list earlier overseas versions with 84 or 99 kWh batteries, 380–465 km WLTP range and around 135 kW DC charging. Those don't apply to the Australian 120 kWh model.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_i