ifications/"},{"title":"Hongqi E-HS9 2026 Review, Specs, Price and Mileage (Brochure) - Auto User Manual","url":"https://autousermanual.com/blogs/hongqi-e-hs9-2026-review-specs-price-and-mileage-brochure/"}]},"Several Australian outlets covering the 11 November 2026 launch agree on the E-HS9's price, range and charging figures.\n\n**Price**\n- Hongqi is selling under the HQ name in Australia. The 2027 E-HS9 has an indicative price below $150,000 before on-road costs, and pre-orders get up to $10,000 cashback.\n- This is not the final price. It's an indicative MSRP before on-road costs, with final pricing still to come. HQ plans one drive-away price per state.\n- Customer deliveries are planned from January 18, 2027.\n\n**Range**\n- A 120 kWh NMC battery gives a claimed WLTP range of 548 km. CATL supplies the battery.\n\n**Charging**\n- It runs on a 400-volt system, and DC fast charging tops out at 140 kW.\n- Hongqi says 10 to 80 per cent takes 48 minutes, and three-phase AC charging goes up to 11 kW. The ports are Type 2 and CCS2.\n\n**Other specs**\n- Dual-motor all-wheel drive makes 411kW and 606Nm, with a claimed 0–100km/h time of 5.5 seconds and a 200km/h top speed.\n- First owners get a 10-year, one million km battery warranty, a seven-year warranty on the rest of the car, and a year of free charging at HQ dealerships.\n\n**Rivals (from CarSauce)**\n- The 2027 Volvo EX90 Ultra Twin Motor Performance costs $134,990 before on-road costs. It has a smaller 111kWh battery but a longer claimed WLTP range of 570km.\n- The 2027 Kia EV9 GT-Line AWD costs $121,000 before on-road costs.\n\n**Older figures to ignore:** Some aggregator sites list earlier overseas versions with 84 or 99 kWh batteries, 380–465 km WLTP range and around 135 kW DC charging. Those don't apply to the Australian 120 kWh model."],"durationSeconds":9.089789304000005,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T57c6PzKD3g84hJLiRAWTa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PdSDabdtBhZq1PN95D4VTa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Xpeng X9 Australia $89,900 WLTP range kWh DC charging\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"XPENG X9 Configurator\",\"url\":\"https://store.xpeng.com/au/configurator/New_X9\"},{\"title\":\"Xpeng X9 seven-seat electric MPV lands in Australia from $89,900\",\"url\":\"https://thebeep.com.au/car-news/2026-xpeng-x9-price-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"XPeng X9 - EV Price, Range & Specs\",\"url\":\"https://evdbau.com/v/xpeng-x9\"},{\"title\":\"XPENG X9 Australia\",\"url\":\"https://www.xpeng.com/au/news/019fa2860f529f8481378a02820600b3\"},{\"title\":\"XPeng X9 Australia Price and Specs\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/reviews/xpeng-x9-price-specs-australia\"},{\"title\":\"2026 XPENG X9 Australia Price and Specs: Electric People Mover From $89,900\",\"url\":\"https://carsauce.com/news/2026-xpeng-x9-australia-price-specs\"},{\"title\":\"2026 XPeng X9 Australia: Price, Specs and Range\",\"url\":\"https://www.evee.com.au/blog/2026-xpeng-x9-australia-price-specs-range/\"},{\"title\":\"Xpeng launches X9 luxury people mover in Australia, priced from $89,900 - The Driven IO\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2026/07/21/xpeng-launches-x9-luxury-people-mover-in-australia-priced-from-89900/\"},{\"title\":\"XPENG X9 Australia Price Revealed, Starts From $89,900\",\"url\":\"https://www.cars24.com.au/car-news/xpeng-x9-australia-price-specs-range-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"XPENG X9 Australia Starts at AUD $89,900: Specs, Range & Features\",\"url\":\"https://bijliwaligaadi.com/07/2026/xpeng-x9-australia-price-specs.html/\"}]\n\nThe $89,900 Xpeng X9 is the entry FWD Standard Range model. It has a 94.8 kWh LFP battery, 535 km of WLTP range and DC charging at up to 537 kW.\n\n**Price and launch:** Xpeng announced Australian pricing on 21 July 2026. There are two versions: the X9 FWD Standard Range, with up to 535km WLTP, at AUD $89,900 plus on-road costs, and the X9 AWD Performance, with up to 580km WLTP, at AUD $109,900 plus on-road costs.\n\n**FWD Standard Range ($89,900):** Xpeng's Australian configurator lists 235 kW / 450 Nm, 0–100 km/h in 8.2 s, 535 km WLTP range (R20), a 94.8 kWh (gross) LFP battery, DC charging up to 537 kW (10–80% in 12 min) and 11 kW AC charging. Energy use is 20.2 kWh/100 km (R20), with 6 kW V2L and a CCS2 port. EVDB AU estimates usable battery capacity at 92 kWh, on an 800 V architecture.\n\n**AWD Performance ($109,900):** 370 kW / 640 Nm, 0–100 km/h in 5.9 s, 580 km WLTP range (R20), a 110 kWh (gross) NCM battery, DC charging up to 542 kW (10–80% in 12 min) and 11 kW AC charging. Energy use is 20.8 kWh/100 km (R20).\n\n**Platform:** Both versions use Xpeng's 800V silicon carbide (SiC) high-voltage platform with 5C ultra-fast charging capability.\n\n**Conflicting charging figures:** Xpeng's own launch release ties the 542 kW peak to the AWD Performance variant. EVee also gives up to 537kW for the FWD and 542kW for the AWD model. Some outlets say both versions charge at 542 kW, including The Driven (\"Both offer DC charging at up to 542kW\") and Zecar. The 537 kW FWD figure from the official configurator is the more reliable one.\n\n**Competitors:** The Beep notes that at $89,900 the X9 opens just above the Denza D9's $88,185 FWD but well under the Zeekr 009's $115,900 starting price.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3c92312-dcdc-442e-a489-64b089455724","uuid":"d7d4eaef-e306-41c2-b205-3de23a40198e","timestamp":"2026-11-18T12:17:37.825Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Xpeng X9 Australia $89,900 WLTP range kWh DC charging","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01EfusGDNCQJi9ddhxBGSCAA","content":[{"title":"XPENG X9 Configurator","url":"https://store.xpeng.com/au/configurator/New_X9"},{"title":"Xpeng X9 seven-seat electric MPV lands in Australia from $89,900","url":"https://thebeep.com.au/car-news/2026-xpeng-x9-price-australia/"},{"title":"XPeng X9 - EV Price, Range & Specs","url":"https://evdbau.com/v/xpeng-x9"},{"title":"XPENG X9 Australia","url":"https://www.xpeng.com/au/news/019fa2860f529f8481378a02820600b3"},{"title":"XPeng X9 Australia Price and Specs","url":"https://zecar.com/reviews/xpeng-x9-price-specs-australia"},{"title":"2026 XPENG X9 Australia Price and Specs: Electric People Mover From $89,900","url":"https://carsauce.com/news/2026-xpeng-x9-australia-price-specs"},{"title":"2026 XPeng X9 Australia: Price, Specs and Range","url":"https://www.evee.com.au/blog/2026-xpeng-x9-australia-price-specs-range/"},{"title":"Xpeng launches X9 luxury people mover in Australia, priced from $89,900 - The Driven IO","url":"https://thedriven.io/2026/07/21/xpeng-launches-x9-luxury-people-mover-in-australia-priced-from-89900/"},{"title":"XPENG X9 Australia Price Revealed, Starts From $89,900","url":"https://www.cars24.com.au/car-news/xpeng-x9-australia-price-specs-range-2026/"},{"title":"XPENG X9 Australia Starts at AUD $89,900: Specs, Range & Features","url":"https://bijliwaligaadi.com/07/2026/xpeng-x9-australia-price-specs.html/"}]},"The $89,900 Xpeng X9 is the entry FWD Standard Range model. It has a 94.8 kWh LFP battery, 535 km of WLTP range and DC charging at up to 537 kW.\n\n**Price and launch:** Xpeng announced Australian pricing on 21 July 2026. There are two versions: the X9 FWD Standard Range, with up to 535km WLTP, at AUD $89,900 plus on-road costs, and the X9 AWD Performance, with up to 580km WLTP, at AUD $109,900 plus on-road costs.\n\n**FWD Standard Range ($89,900):** Xpeng's Australian configurator lists 235 kW / 450 Nm, 0–100 km/h in 8.2 s, 535 km WLTP range (R20), a 94.8 kWh (gross) LFP battery, DC charging up to 537 kW (10–80% in 12 min) and 11 kW AC charging. Energy use is 20.2 kWh/100 km (R20), with 6 kW V2L and a CCS2 port. EVDB AU estimates usable battery capacity at 92 kWh, on an 800 V architecture.\n\n**AWD Performance ($109,900):** 370 kW / 640 Nm, 0–100 km/h in 5.9 s, 580 km WLTP range (R20), a 110 kWh (gross) NCM battery, DC charging up to 542 kW (10–80% in 12 min) and 11 kW AC charging. Energy use is 20.8 kWh/100 km (R20).\n\n**Platform:** Both versions use Xpeng's 800V silicon carbide (SiC) high-voltage platform with 5C ultra-fast charging capability.\n\n**Conflicting charging figures:** Xpeng's own launch release ties the 542 kW peak to the AWD Performance variant. EVee also gives up to 537kW for the FWD and 542kW for the AWD model. Some outlets say both versions charge at 542 kW, including The Driven (\"Both offer DC charging at up to 542kW\") and Zecar. The 537 kW FWD figure from the official configurator is the more reliable one.\n\n**Competitors:** The Beep notes that at $89,900 the X9 opens just above the Denza D9's $88,185 FWD but well under the Zeekr 009's $115,900 starting price."],"durationSeconds":10.79704691199999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PdSDabdtBhZq1PN95D4VTa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
