{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HSZhNQ5r6WabpchdhrLwd6","type":"tool_result","content":"# XPENG X9 Australia: Per-Variant Specs\n\n| Spec | X9 FWD Standard Range | X9 AWD Performance |\n|---|---|---|\n| Price | \"AUD $89,900 plus on road costs\" | \"AUD $109,900 plus on road costs\" |\n| Battery | \"94.8kWh LFP battery (Standard Range)\" | \"110kWh NCM battery (AWD Performance)\" |\n| WLTP range | \"up to 535km WLTP\" | \"up to 580km WLTP\" |\n| Peak DC | Not stated for this variant | \"up to 542kW on the AWD Performance variant\" |\n| 10–80% time | Not tied to this variant* | \"in as little as 12 minutes, under test conditions\" |\n| AC charging | \"11kW AC charging\" (not split by variant) | Same, \"11kW AC charging\" |\n| Drivetrain | FWD (from the variant name) | AWD (from the variant name) |\n| Seats | \"seven-seat\" | \"seven-seat\" |\n\n*The 12-minute figure appears in the same sentence as the AWD's 542kW peak. The release never gives a charge time for the FWD model.\n\n**Other notes:**\n- The page lists \"Up to 370kW / 640Nm\" without naming a variant.\n- It gives \"0–100km/h in 5.9 seconds (AWD)\".\n\n**Release date:** \"Melbourne, 21 July 2026\"\n\n**Orders:** Open. The release says \"Orders are now open through authorised XPENG dealers across Australia,\" and deliveries are \"commencing shortly.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3c92312-dcdc-442e-a489-64b089455724","uuid":"0df8e7e5-e318-4031-95d3-aca109f00ff4","timestamp":"2026-11-18T12:17:50.777Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":362113,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# XPENG X9 Australia: Per-Variant Specs\n\n| Spec | X9 FWD Standard Range | X9 AWD Performance |\n|---|---|---|\n| Price | \"AUD $89,900 plus on road costs\" | \"AUD $109,900 plus on road costs\" |\n| Battery | \"94.8kWh LFP battery (Standard Range)\" | \"110kWh NCM battery (AWD Performance)\" |\n| WLTP range | \"up to 535km WLTP\" | \"up to 580km WLTP\" |\n| Peak DC | Not stated for this variant | \"up to 542kW on the AWD Performance variant\" |\n| 10–80% time | Not tied to this variant* | \"in as little as 12 minutes, under test conditions\" |\n| AC charging | \"11kW AC charging\" (not split by variant) | Same, \"11kW AC charging\" |\n| Drivetrain | FWD (from the variant name) | AWD (from the variant name) |\n| Seats | \"seven-seat\" | \"seven-seat\" |\n\n*The 12-minute figure appears in the same sentence as the AWD's 542kW peak. The release never gives a charge time for the FWD model.\n\n**Other notes:**\n- The page lists \"Up to 370kW / 640Nm\" without naming a variant.\n- It gives \"0–100km/h in 5.9 seconds (AWD)\".\n\n**Release date:** \"Melbourne, 21 July 2026\"\n\n**Orders:** Open. The release says \"Orders are now open through authorised XPENG dealers across Australia,\" and deliveries are \"commencing shortly.\"","durationMs":8092,"url":"https://www.xpeng.com/au/news/019fa2860f529f8481378a02820600b3"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HSZhNQ5r6WabpchdhrLwd6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
