{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QjPgje7V1njYxrzsx3sQ6v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Abarth 500e Australia discontinued 2026 Abarth 600e Australia launch\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Fiat drops its last passenger cars in Australia leaving only vans\",\"url\":\"https://thebeep.com.au/car-news/fiat-500e-abarth-500e-axed-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Abarth 600e debuts - carsales.com.au\",\"url\":\"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/2025-abarth-600e-debuts-144502/\"},{\"title\":\"Fiat edging closer to Australian exit - carsales.com.au\",\"url\":\"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/fiat-edging-closer-to-australian-exit-152521/\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Abarth 600e Scorpionissima unleashed - carsales.com.au\",\"url\":\"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/2025-abarth-600e-scorpionissima-unleashed-147820/\"},{\"title\":\"Fiat drops the 500e and Abarth 500e in Australia as its future remains uncertain - ClubAlfa Global\",\"url\":\"https://www.clubalfa.it/en/fiat-drops-the-500e-and-abarth-500e-in-australia-as-its-future-remains-uncertain-41832\"},{\"title\":\"Abarth 500e arrives in Australia - carsales.com.au\",\"url\":\"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/abarth-500e-arrives-in-australia-144752/\"},{\"title\":\"The petrol-powered Abarth 500 has been discontinued after 16 years\",\"url\":\"https://www.evo.co.uk/abarth/595-hatchback/207088/the-petrol-powered-abarth-500-has-been-discontinued-after-16-years\"},{\"title\":\"Fiat Edges Closer to Leaving Australia as EV Imports Are Suspended\",\"url\":\"https://autoakhbar.com/fiat-australia-exit-2026-ev-imports-suspended/\"},{\"title\":\"The Slow Death of Stellantis Down Under with Fiat 500e Gone\",\"url\":\"https://gaycarboys.com/stellantis-fiat-500e-abarth-australia-gone/\"},{\"title\":\"Abarth 600e review\",\"url\":\"https://www.evo.co.uk/abarth/600e\"}]\n\nThe Abarth 500e has stopped being imported to Australia, and I found nothing confirming an Australian launch for the Abarth 600e.\n\n**Abarth 500e no longer imported (July 2026)**\n- Fiat has stopped importing the Fiat 500e and Abarth 500e, and Stellantis says it doesn't plan to order more. Dealer stock had almost sold out by late July. Remaining stock has almost sold out. At that point Fiat's stock locator showed four new 500e and nine Abarth 500e cars nationally.\n- Stellantis said the cars \"have now largely been sold through,\" and the company is \"not planning additional orders\" while it evaluates \"future product opportunities for the local market.\"\n- Sales had dropped to just 13 vehicles in June 2026. Fiat passenger car sales were down 30.4% to 144 units.\n- The Abarth 500e launched here in 2024 at around $64,000 driveaway before Stellantis stripped $20,000 out of it to move stock. Its launch price was $58,900 plus on-road costs.\n- Fiat Professional still sells the Ducato and Scudo vans, but no new Fiat or Abarth passenger models have been confirmed. Fiat hasn't formally left Australia, and Stellantis says it remains committed to the market.\n\n**Abarth 600e in Australia**\n- When it was revealed (about 2023/24), carsales reported the car isn't on Fiat Australia's radar. It said Australia has been unofficially ruled out due to being a low-volume right-hand drive market.\n- A later carsales article said neither the 600e nor the Scorpionissima version has been confirmed for Australia at the time of writing, but it's though that could change in the coming months.\n- None of the 2026 reports mention an Australian 600e launch.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3c92312-dcdc-442e-a489-64b089455724","uuid":"14343f99-a303-4885-96b0-e4987da84a55","timestamp":"2026-11-18T12:19:57.317Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Abarth 500e Australia discontinued 2026 Abarth 600e Australia launch","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CwGk8MCJAQaAxhsAuC5BKQ","content":[{"title":"Fiat drops its last passenger cars in Australia leaving only vans","url":"https://thebeep.com.au/car-news/fiat-500e-abarth-500e-axed-australia/"},{"title":"2025 Abarth 600e debuts - carsales.com.au","url":"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/2025-abarth-600e-debuts-144502/"},{"title":"Fiat edging closer to Australian exit - carsales.com.au","url":"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/fiat-edging-closer-to-australian-exit-152521/"},{"title":"2025 Abarth 600e Scorpionissima unleashed - carsales.com.au","url":"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/2025-abarth-600e-scorpionissima-unleashed-147820/"},{"title":"Fiat drops the 500e and Abarth 500e in Australia as its future remains uncertain - ClubAlfa Global","url":"https://www.clubalfa.it/en/fiat-drops-the-500e-and-abarth-500e-in-australia-as-its-future-remains-uncertain-41832"},{"title":"Abarth 500e arrives in Australia - carsales.com.au","url":"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/abarth-500e-arrives-in-australia-144752/"},{"title":"The petrol-powered Abarth 500 has been discontinued after 16 years","url":"https://www.evo.co.uk/abarth/595-hatchback/207088/the-petrol-powered-abarth-500-has-been-discontinued-after-16-years"},{"title":"Fiat Edges Closer to Leaving Australia as EV Imports Are Suspended","url":"https://autoakhbar.com/fiat-australia-exit-2026-ev-imports-suspended/"},{"title":"The Slow Death of Stellantis Down Under with Fiat 500e Gone","url":"https://gaycarboys.com/stellantis-fiat-500e-abarth-australia-gone/"},{"title":"Abarth 600e review","url":"https://www.evo.co.uk/abarth/600e"}]},"The Abarth 500e has stopped being imported to Australia, and I found nothing confirming an Australian launch for the Abarth 600e.\n\n**Abarth 500e no longer imported (July 2026)**\n- Fiat has stopped importing the Fiat 500e and Abarth 500e, and Stellantis says it doesn't plan to order more. Dealer stock had almost sold out by late July. Remaining stock has almost sold out. At that point Fiat's stock locator showed four new 500e and nine Abarth 500e cars nationally.\n- Stellantis said the cars \"have now largely been sold through,\" and the company is \"not planning additional orders\" while it evaluates \"future product opportunities for the local market.\"\n- Sales had dropped to just 13 vehicles in June 2026. Fiat passenger car sales were down 30.4% to 144 units.\n- The Abarth 500e launched here in 2024 at around $64,000 driveaway before Stellantis stripped $20,000 out of it to move stock. Its launch price was $58,900 plus on-road costs.\n- Fiat Professional still sells the Ducato and Scudo vans, but no new Fiat or Abarth passenger models have been confirmed. Fiat hasn't formally left Australia, and Stellantis says it remains committed to the market.\n\n**Abarth 600e in Australia**\n- When it was revealed (about 2023/24), carsales reported the car isn't on Fiat Australia's radar. It said Australia has been unofficially ruled out due to being a low-volume right-hand drive market.\n- A later carsales article said neither the 600e nor the Scorpionissima version has been confirmed for Australia at the time of writing, but it's though that could change in the coming months.\n- None of the 2026 reports mention an Australian 600e launch."],"durationSeconds":9.118428551999969,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QjPgje7V1njYxrzsx3sQ6v","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
