{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RG88HkB7uZA913ymdVLFtf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"chery.com.au E5 Ultimate specifications battery kWh DC charging\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Chery E5 Australia: The Budget Electric SUV Disrupting the Market - evee AU - Electric Car Rental\",\"url\":\"https://www.evee.com.au/blog/chery-e5-australia-budget-electric-suv-review/\"},{\"title\":\"Chery E5 - EV Price, Range & Specs\",\"url\":\"https://evdbau.com/v/chery-e5\"},{\"title\":\"Chery E5 Ultimate (2024 - 2026) EV Specifications\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/electric-vehicles/chery/e5/2024/ultimate\"},{\"title\":\"Chery E5 Ultimate Charging Guide: Time, Speed, Cost & Charger Type\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/ev-charging-guides/chery/e5/2024/ultimate\"},{\"title\":\"Chery E5 Price, Range & Specs Australia\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/electric-vehicles/chery/e5\"},{\"title\":\"Chery E5\",\"url\":\"https://ev-wiki.org/chery/e5\"},{\"title\":\"Chery E5 2026 Ultimate Pricing & Specifications - carsales\",\"url\":\"https://www.carsales.com.au/research/chery/e5/2026/ultimate/\"},{\"title\":\"Chery E5 2025 Ultimate Pricing & Specifications - carsales\",\"url\":\"https://www.carsales.com.au/research/chery/e5/2025/ultimate/\"},{\"title\":\"Chery E5 — Grokipedia\",\"url\":\"https://grokipedia.com/page/chery_e5\"},{\"title\":\"Chery E5 Price, Specs & Variants\",\"url\":\"https://thebeep.com.au/cars/chery/e5/\"}]\n\nThe search didn't return a page from chery.com.au itself, so these numbers come from third-party Australian spec sites. They don't all agree, because the E5 Ultimate's battery and charging specs changed between model years.\n\n**Earlier cars (MY24/MY25): 61.1 kWh battery, 80 kW DC**\n- Carsales lists the 2025 E5 Ultimate with a 61.1 kWh high-voltage battery (165.0 Ah) and a DC charging time of 28 min. The motor makes 150kW and 340Nm, accelerating the E5 to 100km/h in 7.6 seconds. Charging from 30 to 80 per cent takes 28 minutes, and the claimed NEDC and WLTP ranges are 460km and 430km.\n- Zecar lists 61.1 kWh LFP (60.5 kWh usable) and up to 80 kW DC (10–80% in 39 minutes) and 9.9 kW AC (0–100% in 6 hrs 54 mins). It uses a Type 2 plug for AC charging and a CCS connector for DC fast charging.\n\n**Later cars (MY26 and on): 58.9 kWh battery, faster DC charging**\n- Carsales lists the 2026 E5 Ultimate MY26 with 155kW listed against \"DC Charging Time (at Max kW)\", a 30 min DC charging time, 163.5 Ah, and a 58.9 kWh battery. The 155kW figure seems to be the DC charging rate, since the motor is still rated at 150kW.\n- EVDB says vehicles built before mid 2025 had a peak DC charge rate of 80 kW, and Model Year 2025.5 has a 155 kW rate. Its own Ultimate spec table still shows 64 kWh nominal / 61 kWh usable and 80 kW DC, which doesn't match.\n- EV-wiki gives the Ultimate MY26 a 58.9 kWh battery, 130 kW max DC, 430 km WLTP range.\n- Grokipedia, a less reliable source, says the Australian version received a battery capacity adjustment to 58.9 kWh and power increase to 155 kW in September 2025.\n- TheBeep also lists the current Ultimate with a 58.9 kWh battery and 430 km WLTP range.\n\n**What every source agrees on:** 430 km WLTP range, front-wheel drive, LFP battery, and 0–100 km/h in 7.6 s.\n\n**Still unresolved:** whether peak DC charging on the current car is 130 kW or 155 kW. Only the official chery.com.au spec sheet or brochure would settle it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3c92312-dcdc-442e-a489-64b089455724","uuid":"3d38c933-f197-41b3-b009-b4f672e99dc3","timestamp":"2026-11-18T12:20:44.508Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"chery.com.au E5 Ultimate specifications battery kWh DC charging","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Sv1LiE8gQfr1XWLwDzdmsk","content":[{"title":"Chery E5 Australia: The Budget Electric SUV Disrupting the Market - evee AU - Electri