kW listed against \"DC Charging Time (at Max kW)\", a 30 min DC charging time, 163.5 Ah, and a 58.9 kWh battery. The 155kW figure seems to be the DC charging rate, since the motor is still rated at 150kW.\n- EVDB says vehicles built before mid 2025 had a peak DC charge rate of 80 kW, and Model Year 2025.5 has a 155 kW rate. Its own Ultimate spec table still shows 64 kWh nominal / 61 kWh usable and 80 kW DC, which doesn't match.\n- EV-wiki gives the Ultimate MY26 a 58.9 kWh battery, 130 kW max DC, 430 km WLTP range.\n- Grokipedia, a less reliable source, says the Australian version received a battery capacity adjustment to 58.9 kWh and power increase to 155 kW in September 2025.\n- TheBeep also lists the current Ultimate with a 58.9 kWh battery and 430 km WLTP range.\n\n**What every source agrees on:** 430 km WLTP range, front-wheel drive, LFP battery, and 0–100 km/h in 7.6 s.\n\n**Still unresolved:** whether peak DC charging on the current car is 130 kW or 155 kW. Only the official chery.com.au spec sheet or brochure would settle it."],"durationSeconds":11.151556977000029,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RG88HkB7uZA913ymdVLFtf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
