{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAPNsCiB3qrFeZnocJkf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TeJpMnCg7a9xBEnfuvxWz5","name":"mcp__safeoutputs__create_pull_request","input":{"title":"Add the MG U9 EV, Xpeng X9, Deepal E07 and Leapmotor B05; Alfa Junior range; Fiat and Abarth 500e no longer sold new","branch":"catalogue/2026-11-18-u9-x9-e07-b05","body":"Six new entries for four EVs now on sale, one WLTP correction, and two cars marked as no longer sold new. Only `vehicles.json` changes, and validation passes (232 vehicles, every id on main kept).\n\n| Change | Old → new | Source and exact figure |\n|---|---|---|\n| **New:** `mg-u9-2026`, MGU9 EV 4x4 dual-cab (ute) | — → 99 kWh usable (est.), 430 km, 115 kW DC, 11 kW AC, 20–80% 42 min | [MG Australia](https://www.mgmotor.com.au/vehicles/mgu9-ev) (18 Nov 2026): \"Available Now\", \"102.2kWh LFP\", \"Up to 430km\", \"115kW peak DC\", \"11kW AC\", \"20-80% in 42 minutes\" |\n| **New:** `xpeng-x9-sr-2026`, X9 FWD Standard Range (van) | — → 92 kWh (est.), 535 km, 537 kW, 11 kW, 10–80% 12 min | [Xpeng AU release, 21 Jul 2026](https://www.xpeng.com/au/news/019fa2860f529f8481378a02820600b3): \"AUD $89,900 plus on road costs\", \"94.8kWh LFP\", \"up to 535km WLTP\", \"Orders are now open\"; [configurator](https://store.xpeng.com/au/configurator/New_X9): \"up to 537 kW\", \"10–80% in 12 min\", \"11 kW\" |\n| **New:** `xpeng-x9-performance-2026`, X9 AWD Performance (van) | — → 106 kWh (est.), 580 km, 542 kW, 11 kW, 10–80% 12 min | Same release: \"AUD $109,900\", \"110kWh NCM\", \"up to 580km WLTP\", \"up to 542kW on the AWD Performance variant\" |\n| **New:** `deepal-e07-rwd-2025`, E07 RWD | — → 86 kWh (est.), 550 km, 240 kW, 7 kW, 30–80% 15 min | [Deepal Australia E07](https://www.deepal.com.au/vehicles/deepal/e07/) (18 Nov 2026): \"89.98kWh NMC battery\", \"550kms\", \"240kW\", \"30 to 80% in just 15 minutes\", \"7kW AC charging\" |\n| **New:** `deepal-e07-awd-2025`, E07 AWD Performance | — → 86 kWh (est.), 510 km, 240 kW, 7 kW, 30–80% 15 min | Same page: \"510kms\", \"DC Charge Time 30%-80%: 15 minutes\" |\n| **New:** `leapmotor-b05-design-2026`, B05 Design Long Range (car) | — → 65 kWh (est.), 482 km, 174 kW, 11 kW, 30–80% 18 min | [The Driven, 2 Jul 2026](https://thedriven.io/2026/07/02/new-leapmotor-b05-electric-hatchback-to-land-in-australia-from-35990-driveway/): \"$39,990 for the Design LR\", \"67.1kWh LFP\", \"up to 482km\", \"fast charging up to 174kW\", \"18 minutes\", \"11kW AC\" |\n| `alfa-romeo-junior-2025` wltpKm | 398 → 407 | [Alfa Romeo Australia Junior](https://www.alfaromeo.com.au/models/junior) (18 Nov 2026): \"54kWh\", \"407km (WLTP)\", \"100kW DC Charging\" |\n| `fiat-500e-2023` untilYear | — → 2026 | Stellantis told The Beep that the cars \"have now largely been sold through\" and it is \"not planning additional orders\" (July 2026). abarth.com.au is now a parked domain. |\n| `abarth-500e-2023` untilYear | — → 2026 | As above |\n\nEvery new or changed entry has `checked: 2026-11-18`. The file's `updated` date is 2026-11-18.\n\n### Things I wasn't sure about\n- **Deepal E07:** Deepal shows prices only through a postcode tool, so the fetch saw \"From XX,XXX RDP\". I counted it as on sale because the page says \"Test drives are available now at your local retailer\" and dealers list stock (e.g. $77,704 drive-away in Queensland). I used body `suv` for this SUV-ute \"multitruck\"; `ute` is arguable. The year is 2025 because dealer listings say MY25.\n- **Leapmotor B05:** the figures come from The Driven, which credits the price to Leapmotor. leapmotor.net/au failed with a certificate error in the sandbox. I added only the Design LR. I left out the Style because its peak DC is unclear: The Driven gives \"up to 174kW\" for the range, and another listing gives 156 kW.\n- **MG U9:** \"102.2kWh\" isn't labelled gross or usable, so I estimated usable at 99 kWh.\n- **Alfa Junior:** the range now comes from the maker page. Its charging notes say \"Overseas model shown, Australian specification may vary\", so I left the existing charge estimate as it was.\n- **Fiat and Abarth end of sale:** this comes from a Stellantis quote reported by The Beep, not from a maker page; fiat.com.au returned 403.\n\n### Not done this run\n- **Re-checked (6):** BYD, Abarth, Alfa Romeo, Deepal, Denza and Fiat. BYD's battery-electric range and the Denza D9 match the file.\n- **Not re-checked:** Tesla, Audi, BMW, Cadillac, Cupra and Ford. Their AU sites returned 403, timed out or failed the certificate check, and tesla.com is off-limits. They are left undated so the next run takes them first.\n- **ROVER:** couldn't be read. Its list loads from content.powerapps.com, which fails the certificate check in the sandbox.\n- **BITRE:** the sheets didn't download (timed out).\n- **Kept as candidates:** HQ/Hongqi E-HS9 (only an indicative price below $150k, deliveries from Jan 2027), Avatr 07L/06T (expressions of interest only), Denza Z9 GT (no AU price) and the Chery E5 (see the separate issue).\n\nNo page asked me to do anything outside the task.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":306,"cache_read_input_tokens":116960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":306,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":32,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3c92312-dcdc-442e-a489-64b089455724","uuid":"8144df14-dadb-407b-94f6-89c9de005de7","timestamp":"2026-11-18T12:23:27.506Z","request_id":"req_011ChAPNs3YM4fMFhMQd7G2D","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TeJpMnCg7a9xBEnfuvxWz5","display_name":"Create Pull Request","server_display_name":"awmg-safeoutputs","tool_name":"create_pull_request"}]}
