{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAPR3DH9G7nYycmkzhDv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I opened one pull request on branch `catalogue/2026-11-18-u9-x9-e07-b05` and one issue. The PR changes only `vehicles.json`; the formatter ran and `validate.mjs` passes (232 vehicles, every id on main kept).\n\n**Pull request: \"Add the MG U9 EV, Xpeng X9, Deepal E07 and Leapmotor B05; Alfa Junior range; Fiat and Abarth 500e no longer sold new\"**\n- **MG U9 EV (`mg-u9-2026`):** a ute with 430 km WLTP and 115 kW DC. MG's page says \"Available Now\".\n- **Xpeng X9:** two entries, FWD Standard Range and AWD Performance. Xpeng's 21 July release gives prices ($89,900 and $109,900) and says orders are open.\n- **Deepal E07:** RWD and AWD entries with 550 km and 510 km WLTP and 240 kW DC. Deepal's page shows the price only as a placeholder, so I counted it as on sale because test drives are available at retailers and dealers list cars in stock. The PR flags this.\n- **Leapmotor B05 Design LR:** 482 km and 174 kW, from The Driven, which credits the price to Leapmotor. Leapmotor's own site failed with a certificate error. I left out the cheaper Style because its peak DC power isn't clear (174 or 156 kW).\n- **Alfa Romeo Junior:** WLTP range changed from 398 to 407 km, the figure on Alfa Romeo's Australian page.\n- **Fiat 500e and Abarth 500e:** `untilYear` set to 2026. Stellantis told The Beep it has stopped ordering them; this isn't from a maker page.\n\nTwo things to know when reviewing:\n- **Usable battery figures are estimates:** for the new cars I worked them out from the published battery sizes, and each `source` says \"est.\".\n- **The earlier run never reached main:** your memory had marked the MG U9, Xpeng X9 and Leapmotor B05 as \"added\", but none were in the file and no pull request existed. I verified them again before adding them.\n\n**Issue: Chery E5.** The owner's Chery lead is the Chery E5, which is the renamed Omoda E5 already in the file as `omoda-e5-2024`. Sources disagree on the current car's battery and peak DC charging (130 or 155 kW, against the file's 80 kW), and Chery's Australian site couldn't be read. I left the cautious 80 kW figure and asked you to decide on a separate 2026 entry and the correct charging figure.\n\n**Not done this run:**\n- **Six makes not re-checked:** Tesla, Audi, BMW, Cadillac, Cupra and Ford. Their sites refused the request, timed out or failed the certificate check, and tesla.com is off-limits. I left them undated so the next run takes them first.\n- **Six makes re-checked:** BYD, Abarth, Alfa Romeo, Deepal, Denza and Fiat. Denza was checked against news reports only, because its site wouldn't load.\n- **ROVER couldn't be read:** its approval list loads from content.powerapps.com, which fails the certificate check here.\n- **BITRE sheets missing:** they didn't download before the run.\n\n**Kept as candidates in memory, not added:**\n- **HQ (Hongqi) E-HS9:** only an indicative price below $150,000, with deliveries from January 2027.\n- **Avatr 07L and 06T:** expressions of interest only.\n- **Denza Z9 GT:** confirmed for Australia but no price yet.\n\nMemory is saved, and no web page tried to give instructions."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":120545,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":331,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3c92312-dcdc-442e-a489-64b089455724","uuid":"83842cbe-c04f-40af-8c21-19de0aa46987","timestamp":"2026-11-18T12:23:48.771Z","request_id":"req_011ChAPR34cAVmuXqxcKgVAk"}
